thag1.104:1.1 starts: How light my body!
thag1.104:1.2 starts: Touched by abundant
thag1.104:1.3 starts: —like a cotton tuft
thag1.104:1.4 starts: it seems to be floating
thag1.110:1.1 starts: Trees on the hilltops
thag1.110:1.2 starts: watered by a new high-rising cloud,
thag1.110:1.3 starts: giving birth to even more goodness
thag1.110:1.4 starts: desiring seclusion,
thag1.114:1.1 starts: For one heavy
thag1.114:1.2 starts: greedy
thag1.114:1.3 starts: while life is wasting away:
thag1.114:1.4 starts: From where will there come
thag1.118:1.1 starts: As if sent by a curse,
thag1.118:1.2 starts: The body seems other,
thag1.118:1.3 starts: I’m still here
thag1.118:1.4 starts: but I remember myself
thag2.9:1.1 starts: At ease sleep the sages
thag2.9:1.2 starts: who
thag2.9:1.3 starts: in whom
thag2.9:1.4 starts: is the truth
thag2.17:1.1 starts: He gains many enemies,
thag2.17:1.2 starts: one who—shaven-headed,
thag2.17:1.3 starts: gains food, drink,
thag2.17:1.4 starts: cloth, lodgings.
